  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nWe propose an adaptive multi-phased optimization strategy that combines deterministic local search with adaptive exploration. The core idea is <entity id=\"e0\">dual-mode local and global optimization</entity> that automatically transitions between near-neighbor refinement (Phase 1) and population-based evolutionary search (Phase 2) based on convergence signals and diversity metrics. Our method maintains a balance between exploitation (fine-tuning) and exploration (diversification) by:\n- Dynamically switching phases based on estimated diversity loss\n- Using gradient-based descent for local refinement\n- Employing wavelet-domain operations to accelerate convolution computations\n- Incorporating frequency-domain analysis as quality metrics\nThis hybrid approach addresses the challenges of high-dimensional optimization while respecting the evaluation budget and coefficient bounds.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nThe optimization targets the exact AC1 upper bound objective:\n    minimize f(x) = (2 * n * max(convolve(a, a))) / (sum(a))\u00b2\nwith a \u2208 [0, 1000]\u207f and sum(a) \u2265 0.01.\n\nThe algorithm features:\n- <entity id=\"e1\">Wavelet-convolution reduction</entity>: Represent sequence as discrete wavelet coefficients plus reconstruction\n- <entity id=\"e2\">Gradient-based refinement</entity>: Uses analytic gradient of the max-convolution operator\n- <entity id=\"e3\">Adaptive population</entity>: Maintaining size based on remaining budget\n- <entity id=\"e4\">Frequency-sparse initialization</entity>: Starts with periodic sequences in the Fourier domain\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nIn code terms:\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.fft import rfft, irfft\nfrom scipy.spatial import distance\n\ndef propose_candidate(seed=42, budget_s=1300, **kwargs):\n    t0 = time.time()\n    deadline = t0 + budget_s/1000  # Scale down for efficient computing (budget_s is in ms)\n    \n    # Load parent sequence (seed)\n    try:\n        parent = np.array(height_sequence_1, dtype=np.float64)\n    except:\n        parent = np.ones(192, dtype=np.float64)\n    \n    n = 192\n    # Adaptive sizing based on timeout budget\n    max_evals = int(budget_s) // 200\n    p_size = min(8, max(4, int(max_evals**0.4)))\n    \n    # Wavelet representation setup\n    from pywt import Wavelet, dwt\n    wavelet_name = \"coif1\"\n    wavelet = Wavelet(wavelet_name)\n    coeffs = dwt(parent, wavelet)\n    rec_orig = pywt.idwt(coeffs, wavelet)[:n]\n    \n    # Mode 1: Phased Local Descent\n    def phase1_descent(x):\n        # Compute initial descent\n        c_size = 5\n        history = [x]\n        for i in range(c_size-1):\n            # Gradient update (analytic gradient)\n            conv = rconvolve(x, x, mode=\"full\")\n            max_idx = np.argmax(conv)\n            # Analytic gradient of max-convolution (unstable!)\n            # We use crutches here: if cost > min_cost record break\n            pass  #Gap ingradingection\n```\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations",
